{
  "_comment": "Notable Deeds: 53 recorded entries worth 20695 Karma Shards in total, of which 20000 comes from the four Part I route completions alone. Both sources behind this list describe themselves as incomplete, so this is a floor rather than the full set.",
  "_mechanics": {
    "where": "Completed deeds are claimed at any Pale Raven~s Perch in Dagsion or at the Shrine of Causality in the Obelisk Chamber.",
    "currency": "Deeds pay Karma Shards.",
    "purpose": "Karma Shards unlock Boons of Salvation, and from Part III they also feed Merge Causality.",
    "completeness": "You do not need every deed to unlock every boon, so a completionist run is optional rather than required.",
    "reminder": "The game may pop up a reminder when a deed completes rather than paying out immediately. The source marks that unverified."
  },
  "_economy": {
    "oneRoute": "One Part I route with every recorded deed comes to about 5,695 shards, of which 5,000 is the route completion itself.",
    "allRoutes": "All four Part I routes come to about 20,695 shards.",
    "knownFirstTierCosts": "The published first-tier boon prices add up to about 5,000 shards for sixteen of the thirty-one boons.",
    "caveat": "Both figures are floors, because one source marks its own list work in progress and the other states outright that it does not list every deed."
  },
  "_openGaps": [
    "No total: no source states how many Notable Deeds the game actually contains.",
    "Every entry is marked unverified by the source that compiled them.",
    "No payout mechanics: where and when shards are credited, and whether the reminder is required, is recorded only loosely."
  ],
